  "methodology_disclosures": {
    "leakage_risk_statement": "Synthetic data generator introduces known typologies with parameterized noise. While deterministic rules capture patterns that align closely with generator logic, unsupervised Isolation Forest evaluates multi-dimensional density distributions without prior knowledge of labels, ensuring unbiased outlier scoring.",
    "zero_day_generalization": "The leave-one-typology-out cross experiment proves that supervised models (XGBoost) fail to recognize zero-day fraud typologies when omitted from training data. Conversely, the hybrid blend and unsupervised Isolation Forest retain high anomaly recall because they flag statistical distance rather than learned boundary rules."
  }
